# The repo root sits directly on top of the data tree (4.2 TB on the cluster), so this file
# is load-bearing: `git add -A` with data/ untracked would try to stage the whole allocation.
# Git does not descend into an ignored directory, so the top-level data/ rule is enough.

# ── controlled-access data — never in git ────────────────────────────────────
# AMP-AD (Synapse) and AMP-PD (GCP) both require their own DUA. A collaborator fetches
# these themselves, on biowulf; the commands are recorded in wgs_core.ipynb §0.
data/

# ── outputs, all regenerable from code + data ────────────────────────────────
clinical_core_out/
logs/

# results/ — everything ignored EXCEPT the eta^2 evidence tables. Those are aggregate (one row
# per ancestry stratum: n, callset count, eta^2 per PC — no IIDs, no genotypes), so they are
# safe to version, and they are the measured justification for the AF-concordance filter.
#
# The 0.984 / 0.757 unfiltered baseline survived its first overwrite only because someone had
# typed the numbers into the project log by hand. "Regenerable from code + data" was true in
# principle and false in practice: regenerating a BASELINE means re-running the step in a state
# that no longer exists. Version the evidence.
#
# The negations are deliberately narrow. results/ also holds retained_samples_manifest.csv,
# which is one row per SAMPLE and must stay out — an earlier draft of this block un-ignored
# results/ wholesale and swept it in.
results/*
!results/pca/
results/pca/*
!results/pca/*_eta2.csv
!results/pca/af_filter_effect*.csv
*.log
slurm-*.out

# ── environment and secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
.venv_backup*/
.env

# ── large binaries: liftOver + its chain file (~20 MB), installed per-machine ─
bin/

# ── prior versions, kept on disk for provenance but not carried in the repo ──
scripts_archive/

# ── python / jupyter / editor artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.DS_Store

# NOT ignored, deliberately:
#   ref/          refFlat.txt (21 MB) + highld_exclude_hg38.bed — small, public, and the
#                 single source of locus coordinates. Versioning it means a fresh checkout on
#                 the cluster can run gene_annot.py with no setup. The large, non-redistributable reference
#                 (fasta, ancestry panel) lives in data/ref/ and is ignored with the rest.
